<!--
  k3s API server audit log decoder.

  Companion to platform/manifests/wazuh-host-agent/ossec.conf.template's
  k3s-audit <localfile> block, which uses <out_format> to tag each line
  with syslog program name "k3s-audit".

  Purpose: CLAIM the message via <program_name> match so Wazuh's built-in
  JSON_Decoder does NOT auto-fire on it. The audit log body starts with
  '{' (k3s emits JSON-Lines) — without this decoder, analysisd's
  content-sniffing JSON parser explodes every event into data.* fields.
  RequestResponse events embed Server-Side Apply field tracking in
  metadata.managedFields.fieldsV1, which uses a literal "." as an object
  key. After flattening that lands as a field named "." in the alert,
  and OpenSearch rejects the document with
  mapper_parsing_exception: field name cannot contain only the character [.]
  silently dropping the alert before it indexes.

  This decoder has NO regex or order — it deliberately extracts nothing.
  Rules 100600 / 100800 / etc. still fire because they use <match>/<regex>
  against full_log text, which is preserved verbatim regardless of decoder.

  If structured audit fields are wanted later (queryable verb/user/resource),
  add a SCOPED child decoder here that extracts ONLY safe keys with explicit
  <regex offset="after_prematch"> — do not switch to plugin_decoder JSON.

  Lives at /var/ossec/etc/decoders/local_decoder_k3s_audit.xml on the
  wazuh-manager pod. Source-of-truth in this repo; deploy via
  platform/components/07n-wazuh-k3s-audit-decoder.sh.
-->
<decoder name="k3s-audit">
  <program_name>^k3s-audit$</program_name>
</decoder>
